<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crusades</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusades</a> were a series of religious wars launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latins">Latin Christians</a> from the late eleventh century, chiefly to capture and hold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> took advantage of the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik Shah</a>. The crusades shaped relations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the Islamic world for centuries.</p></div>
